add('slow4fast','INSPECTED CODE at 75e73db12ff4d37013bb4769b0e081bfc9796bd4: The official documented main_nav.py imports GMapNavAgent, whose _build_model constructs ordinary VLNBert (r2r/agent.py:24–32). No reflection/ExperienceEnhanced integration is present in this agent path. Separate reflection_memory_bank.py:236–252 _call_llm_api returns a fixed mock response; get_experience_embeddings at441–454 returns random placeholder vectors. experience_enhanced_vlnbert.py:121–127 uses character-code placeholder text encoding. Retrieval unions scene/context/action indices and ranks by stored success rate and confidence (reflection_memory_bank.py:415–439). These source findings prevent verification of the paper’s end-to-end learned reflection mechanism from the documented release. They do not establish that reported experiments used these placeholders. Success labels enter saved experience records, but the incomplete integration prevents determining their exact evaluation-time provenance. No API, training, simulator or navigation benchmark was executed. Line references use raw LF numbering; doubled carriage returns in these files can make universal-newline viewers display twice as many lines.', ['README.md','r2r/main_nav.py:1–50','r2r/agent.py:16–36','r2r/reflection_memory_bank.py:236–280,415–456','r2r/experience_enhanced_vlnbert.py:23–95,121–127'], 'Official release inspected; central reflection and text-embedding paths contain explicit placeholders, and documented agent does not integrate them.')
add('uln','INSPECTED CODE BY ASSIGNMENT 05 at 0f251df3ffc6dd9c538d075db8674e6ad54a596b: The released recurrent VLN-BERT implementation feeds attended visual/language feature vectors to the uncertainty MLP, ignoring the score tensors; this differs from the raw-score formulation in paper Eq6 (model.py:865–882). Classifier training uses agreement with a stored rollout-result path, produced by train.py:267–287, through _teacher_action(from_env=False); these labels are not independently verified oracle correctness. Exploration scores explicitly accumulate raw future logits, confirming the lack of cross-state additive-gauge invariance in this scoring path (agent.py:683,754–755,857–892). The first step cannot trigger exploration and at most three events are allowed (1065–1074). Parallel exploration simulators and filtered/spliced reported viewpoints mean physical travel accounting needs a separate matched replay audit; no direction or magnitude of cost error is established. Granularity routing and dual language encoders are present; the exact isolated high-level-encoder freeze/reset phase was not located. Full-method test switches are commented in the launcher and the HAMT implementation remains unreleased according to README. Full exact paths/ranges: evidence/05/uln_code_audit.md. No project code was executed.', ['Assignment 05: evidence/05/uln_code_audit.md; ULN-Rec-VLN-BERT model.py:865–882; agent.py:270–294,620–627,683,754–755,857–892,1065–1074; train.py:267–287; README and launcher'], 'Official recurrent VLN-BERT source independently inspected by05; HAMT release incomplete.')
add('mind_error','INSPECTED CODE: The BEV-based trajectory matcher uses a learned trajectory CLS token, positional encoding and crossmodal encoder, with binary detection and an 80-position localization head (vlnce_baselines/models/bev/vilmodel_cmt.py:687–742). ss_trainer_BEV.py:1755–1789 explicitly says navigation imitation loss is not used to fine-tune the navigator in this phase, and combines binary cross-entropy with per-error token cross-entropy. Ground-truth error sensors supply supervision; evaluation uses sigmoid/ROC-AUC and top-k token predictions. The tokenizer maximum and trajectory representation constrain the scope of localization; this is a trajectory/instruction inconsistency detector, not a causal proof that the language rather than behavior is wrong. README pins Habitat0.1.7 and links model/data resources. Source was inspected, not imported or executed; no detector quality was independently reproduced.', ['README.md','vlnce_baselines/models/bev/vilmodel_cmt.py:687–742','vlnce_baselines/ss_trainer_BEV.py:1755–1789; inspected optimizer/evaluation references at283–318,875–889,1067–1073,1631–1661'])
add('vsi_bench','INSPECTED CODE: lmms_eval/tasks/vsibench/utils.py:48–180 resolves scene videos, builds numeric or multiple-choice prompts, extracts the first response word, computes case-insensitive exact-match for multiple choice and mean relative-accuracy thresholds for numeric answers, averages each task, averages direction difficulty bins, then averages task scores. This is an eight-task macro-average, not navigation success or accuracy over one pooled item list. The repository contains a modified lmms-eval harness and model adapters, not a new model-training algorithm. README warns the released dataset was refined and scores may differ from the paper. Pin both dataset revision and model/prompt/video-sampling settings for comparisons. Models, videos and API inference were not executed.', ['README.md','lmms_eval/tasks/vsibench/utils.py:48–180'])
add('uot','INSPECTED CODE: src/uot/uot.py:85–155 partitions candidate sets, implements the sharpened binary-entropy reward, and supports average or maximum future-child aggregation. The executable reward has the correct entropy minus signs absent from the printed equation. However, avg_expected multiplies its child average by a branch probability and expected_reward multiplies again by that branch probability (115–147); paper-equivalent expected-utility interpretation should be checked before using this implementation as a calibrated decision rule. idiv_reward also assigns reward1 when the two partition cardinalities differ by one (103–107). These are deterministic code semantics, not evidence of benchmark impact. README includes API-dependent closed models and an open-set possibility-update protocol. No API interaction or model output was executed.', ['README.md','src/uot/uot.py:85–155'])
add('explore_confident','INSPECTED CODE: The official explore-eqa release provides a Habitat exploration pipeline, TSDF mapping, VLM answer/relevancy scoring, semantic frontier selection and question-generation scripts. run_vlm_exp.py:197–213 scores answer options and confidence about the current view, while339–366 aggregates the recorded trajectory by relevancy-weighted or highest-relevancy prediction. A full-tree search finds no conformal calibration/prediction-set intersection or calibrated stopping implementation in the released Python source, and the pinned tree contains no notebooks. README documents semantic-exploration and CLIP exploration commands and the 500-question HM-EQA dataset. Therefore the paper’s conformal stopping guarantee remains paper evidence; the released pipeline alone does not reproduce that guarantee. This is bounded to the pinned official release, not a claim no code exists elsewhere. HM3D access, VLM weights and simulator execution were not attempted.', ['README.md','run_vlm_exp.py:197–213,339–366','Pinned repository tree and source search for conformal/calibration/quantile'], 'Exploration/answer source inspected; calibrated stopping implementation not found in the pinned official release.')
